# --- macOS ---
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Icon?
._*

# --- Superpowers SDD artifacts ---
# This block is a DENYLIST, not an allowlist. Once git is allowed to descend
# into .superpowers/sdd/<slug>/, everything inside that slug is tracked EXCEPT
# the bulk patterns re-ignored at the bottom. A new artifact type added under a
# slug is therefore tracked by default and needs no edit here.
.superpowers/*
!.superpowers/sdd/
.superpowers/sdd/*
!.superpowers/sdd/*/
# The five negations below are currently REDUNDANT: `.superpowers/sdd/*` matches
# only one level deep, so files inside `<slug>/` were never ignored to begin
# with. They are kept deliberately — they document which artifacts we consider
# durable project knowledge, and they become load-bearing the moment the base
# pattern above is ever tightened (e.g. to `.superpowers/sdd/**`).
!.superpowers/sdd/**/progress.md
!.superpowers/sdd/**/task-*-report.md
!.superpowers/sdd/**/task-*-review.md
!.superpowers/sdd/**/*-design.md
!.superpowers/sdd/**/*-plan.md
# ORDERING IS LOAD-BEARING: these three patterns must stay AFTER the negations
# above. Git applies the last matching pattern, so moving them earlier would let
# a `!` line re-admit them. They are what keeps sibling worktrees' ~190 MB of
# review diffs and review packages out of history when those branches
# eventually merge with this one. Do not reorder this block.
.superpowers/**/review-*.diff
.superpowers/**/*-review-package.md
.superpowers/**/*.diff

#Fastlane api
